Makes it much easier to follow.

915
00:44:43,710 --> 00:44:45,150
Yeah, it creates visual order.

916
00:44:45,430 --> 00:44:49,670
It's all about making those visuals work for you, not against you.

917
00:44:49,750 --> 00:44:51,780
They should complement your message, make it stronger.

918
00:44:52,160 --> 00:44:55,500
Okay, how to keep people engaged from start to finish.

919
00:44:55,580 --> 00:44:56,620
That can be tough.

920
00:44:56,640 --> 00:44:59,620
They were big on that strong opening, you know, grab them right away.

921
00:45:00,300 --> 00:45:04,590
An intriguing fact, a bold statement, something that makes them go, whoa.

922
00:45:04,850 --> 00:45:06,410
First impressions are everything.

923
00:45:06,510 --> 00:45:09,430
Keep them on their toes with little interactive moments throughout too.

924
00:45:10,140 --> 00:45:13,720
Quick polls, questions, you know, just to shake things up.

925
00:45:13,700 --> 00:45:15,600
It breaks the monotony, gets people involved.

926
00:45:15,680 --> 00:45:16,950
And vary your pace.

927
00:45:17,180 --> 00:45:17,390
Right.

928
00:45:17,910 --> 00:45:19,870
Sometimes speed up a little to add energy.

929
00:45:19,910 --> 00:45:23,030
Other times slow down to emphasize something important.

930
00:45:23,070 --> 00:45:24,390
Yeah, like a good song.

931
00:45:24,510 --> 00:45:25,880
You've got to have dynamics.

932
00:45:26,020 --> 00:45:27,540
Rhetorical questions, they're good too.

933
00:45:27,720 --> 00:45:28,560
Get people thinking.

934
00:45:28,840 --> 00:45:29,800
Engages their brains.

935
00:45:30,100 --> 00:45:31,260
And real life stories.

936
00:45:31,860 --> 00:45:32,670
Always a winner.

937
00:45:32,790 --> 00:45:33,810
Yeah, makes it relatable.

938
00:45:33,910 --> 00:45:34,610
Makes it stick.

939
00:45:34,630 --> 00:45:35,970
A stressed vocal variety.

940
00:45:36,050 --> 00:45:39,040
Don't be afraid to, like, change your pitch, your volume.

941
00:45:39,200 --> 00:45:40,840
Makes you more interesting to listen to.

942
00:45:40,820 --> 00:45:59,160
props if you use them use them sparingly make sure they have a purpose not just random stuff they should enhance not distract little humor if it fits but you know be careful with that definitely read the room then make it personal connect to your audience's world their experiences

943
00:45:59,180 --> 00:46:01,540
People pay attention when they feel like it's about them.

944
00:46:01,640 --> 00:46:04,930
Give them a little teaser too about something cool that's coming up later.

945
00:46:05,010 --> 00:46:06,530
You know, build anticipation.

946
00:46:06,770 --> 00:46:07,330
Keeps them hooked.

947
00:46:07,570 --> 00:46:12,280
Little recaps can be good too, just to remind people where you've been, how it all connects.

948
00:46:12,300 --> 00:46:14,800
It brings everyone back together, makes sure no one's lost.

949
00:46:14,820 --> 00:46:21,910
And you, the presenter, they were big on confident posture, moving around the stage purposefully.

950
00:46:21,950 --> 00:46:23,030
Owning the space.

951
00:46:23,110 --> 00:46:27,160
Dramatic pauses, they're good too, just before you reveal something important.

952
00:46:27,140 --> 00:46:28,080
Adds impact.

