00:46:28,220 --> 00:46:30,080
And most importantly, watch your audience.

954
00:46:30,460 --> 00:46:31,220
Are they engaged?

955
00:46:31,700 --> 00:46:32,110
Bored?

956
00:46:32,790 --> 00:46:33,810
Adjust if you need to.

957
00:46:33,890 --> 00:46:34,630
Read the room.

958
00:46:35,310 --> 00:46:38,030
So many moving parts to keeping people engaged.

959
00:46:38,230 --> 00:46:40,450
It's about creating an experience.

960
00:46:40,470 --> 00:46:43,100
Speaking of experience, let's talk practice.

961
00:46:43,320 --> 00:46:45,220
These guys, they were big on practice.

962
00:46:45,640 --> 00:46:48,600
Multiple sessions, really getting comfortable with your material.

963
00:46:48,720 --> 00:46:51,190
Practice makes perfect, or as close as you can get.

964
00:46:51,490 --> 00:46:52,450
Time yourself, too.

965
00:46:52,670 --> 00:46:55,090
Make sure you're not going to run out of time or drag on forever.

966
00:46:55,410 --> 00:46:56,470
Respect the clock.

