00:47:23,570 --> 00:47:25,210
Preparation for the real world.

979
00:47:25,290 --> 00:47:29,740
Practice varying your pitch, your volume, so you don't sound like a robot.

980
00:47:29,760 --> 00:47:30,540
Keep it dynamic.

981
00:47:30,640 --> 00:47:32,600
If you're going to use humor, practice that too.

982
00:47:32,700 --> 00:47:33,500
Make sure it lands.

983
00:47:33,640 --> 00:47:34,440
You don't want crickets.

984
00:47:34,660 --> 00:47:35,760
Streamline your notes.

985
00:47:36,050 --> 00:47:37,710
Get rid of anything that's going to trip you up.

986
00:47:37,890 --> 00:47:38,490
Keep it simple.

987
00:47:38,870 --> 00:47:42,470
Work on your enunciation, especially if you're using technical jargon.

988
00:47:43,010 --> 00:47:44,390
Be crystal clear.

989
00:47:44,680 --> 00:47:46,280
Make sure every word is understood.

990
00:47:46,340 --> 00:47:49,160
Pace yourself so you don't rush through the important stuff.

991
00:47:49,180 --> 00:47:52,120
Give those key points the space they need to breathe.

992
00:47:52,360 --> 00:47:53,160
And this is interesting.

993
00:47:53,340 --> 00:47:55,140
Practice your Q&A answers, too.

994
00:47:55,610 --> 00:47:55,800
Yeah.

995
00:47:55,970 --> 00:47:57,210
Anticipate those questions.

996
00:47:57,590 --> 00:47:58,930
Have some responses ready to go.

997
00:47:58,970 --> 00:48:01,520
Do a full dress rehearsal, like the whole thing.

998
00:48:01,580 --> 00:48:02,460
Run it like it's showtime.

999
00:48:02,720 --> 00:48:04,000
And be open to feedback.

1000
00:48:04,160 --> 00:48:05,890
Tweak things based on what you learn.

1001
00:48:06,110 --> 00:48:08,050
It's a process of continuous improvement.

1002
00:48:08,230 --> 00:48:10,030
So much goes into a great presentation.

1003
00:48:10,070 --> 00:48:10,760
It's amazing.

1004
00:48:10,920 --> 00:48:12,140
It's definitely a craft.

1005
00:48:12,220 --> 00:48:13,160
Okay, objections.

1006
00:48:13,640 --> 00:48:17,190
What if someone disagrees with you or challenges your ideas?

1007
00:48:17,810 --> 00:48:21,660
They were big on staying calm, having a plan for how to handle that.

1008
00:48:21,680 --> 00:48:23,900
Yeah, it's easy to get flustered, but you got to keep your cool.

1009
00:48:24,240 --> 00:48:26,020
Acknowledge their viewpoint, first of all.

1010
00:48:26,320 --> 00:48:27,210
Makes them feel heard.

1011
00:48:27,450 --> 00:48:28,430
Shows respect.

1012
00:48:28,450 --> 00:48:31,410
And have some counter arguments, ready, you know, based on facts.

1013
00:48:31,650 --> 00:48:33,320
Be prepared to back up what you're saying.

1014
00:48:33,450 --> 00:48:40,200
They suggested trying to rephrase the objection as a question turns it into more of a conversation.

1015
00:48:40,260 --> 00:48:41,200
Diffuses the tension.

1016
00:48:41,360 --> 00:48:44,040
And watch your body language even when you're getting grilled.

1017
00:48:44,080 --> 00:48:46,710
Stay calm, collected, confident.

1018
00:48:46,790 --> 00:48:50,530
Try to find common ground, emphasize those shared goals.

1019
00:48:50,790 --> 00:48:52,240
Focus on what you agree on.

1020
00:48:52,480 --> 00:48:55,580
Always thank them for the question, even if it's tough.

1021
00:48:55,600 --> 00:48:57,040
Again, it's about respect.

1022
00:48:57,440 --> 00:49:00,150
Have some backup data ready, just in case you need to go deeper.

1023
00:49:00,550 --> 00:49:02,410
It shows you've done your due diligence.

1024
00:49:02,660 --> 00:49:04,040
Be concise in your responses.

1025
00:49:04,140 --> 00:49:04,740
Don't ramble.

1026
00:49:05,590 --> 00:49:06,910
Respect people's time.

1027
00:49:07,510 --> 00:49:11,840
If the objection's taking you off track, gently steer it back to the main point.

1028
00:49:12,200 --> 00:49:12,980
Stay in control.

1029
00:49:13,200 --> 00:49:15,340
And practice, even those tough scenarios.

1030
00:49:15,820 --> 00:49:19,690
Yeah, mental rehearsal can be just as important as the actual practice.

1031
00:49:19,710 --> 00:49:22,290
Handling objections, it's like a skill in itself, isn't it?

1032
00:49:22,430 --> 00:49:22,710
It is.

1033
00:49:22,890 --> 00:49:24,060
It's about communication.

1034
00:49:24,080 --> 00:49:25,480
It's about diplomacy.

1035
00:49:25,730 --> 00:49:26,470
Almost there.

